# Hook scripts are executed by Git for Windows' bash. A CRLF-terminated
# shebang makes the exec layer look for an interpreter literally named
# "bash\r":
#
#   $ /usr/bin/env $'bash\r' -c 'echo x'
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory      exit=127
#
# On pre-commit that non-zero exit BLOCKS EVERY COMMIT on that machine, with
# an error message that makes no sense to the person hitting it.
#
# This repo has core.autocrlf=true and it is demonstrably converting
# (`git ls-files --eol` reports package.json as i/lf w/crlf), so without this
# rule a fresh clone would check these hooks out with CRLF.
#
# Scoped to this directory rather than the root .gitattributes so it is a
# brand-new file that no outstanding branch can conflict on.
* text eol=lf
